  "formulas": {
    "public": "G*f*ca*m; m is NEW public funding per CA donor core dollar, not existing reimbursements",
    "children": "(G*f+public)/C; C is complete delivery cash per clinically indicated delivered child including allocated failed screens/exams/noncompletion",
    "discounted_years": "integral 0..T of (1+r)^(-t) dt",
    "health": "base_N*A*(gap*wear*u*D(T)-shared_harm)*discount(d) + match_N*A*(gap*wear*u*D(T)-shared_harm)*discount(d) - independent_donor_harm; geography applied separately by tranche",
    "cost": "G+new_public+N*in_kind; no healthcare savings or baseline public money added",
    "ratios": "10*cost/health only when health>0, otherwise null",
    "geography": "base shared health times ordinary Bay/SF share + California match shared health times CA-conditional Bay/SF share - independent donor harm times ordinary Bay/SF share",
    "timing": "d is donation-to-dispensing calendar delay; D(T) integrates health for T years AFTER dispensing; shared harm at dispensing; independent donor harm at donation. Complete nominal committed costs at donation."
  },
  "boundaries": [
    "All numeric scenario inputs are analyst judgments except gift and chosen discount convention. No claimed trial utility calibration.",
    "Cost includes completed-child delivery and allocated upstream attrition; no extra completion probability.",
    "Core fraction funds delivery; remaining fraction funds shared institutional overhead, fundraising and unquantified research/advocacy; complete gift remains numerator.",
    "A is donor-to-net-new-service financial replacement; gap is absent adequate correction among those extra recipients. Wear is corrected-time fraction, not separate efficacy multiplier.",
    "T is finite time before no-new-gift care catches up, with no lifetime educational or amblyopia tail. Two-year scenario requires replacement/follow-up cash in C.",
    "Benefit utility averages refractive severity among delivered children; not every child is assumed visually impaired by WHO criteria.",
    "Public-match sensitivity is hypothetical new cash, conditional on authority, donor eligibility, claims and capacity; no automatic match for unrestricted gifts. No additionality multiplication applied to its gross resource accounting.",
    "Unique child-course only; second pairs/replacements protect duration rather than create extra utility. No PHC adult or partner glasses duplicate credit.",
    "Base Bay/SF resident shares and matching-tranche conditional California resident shares are separate analyst priors, not observed beneficiary fractions. Matching cash funds only California care; no cross-state fungibility benefit claimed.",
    "Donation-to-dispensing delay is an explicit judgment: central1.5months, favorable1month, pessimistic3months. Primary reports weeks after examination, not after gift. Care advantage T starts at dispensing and ends d+T; no benefit during waiting. Shared harm at d; donor-independent harm at0."
  ],
